{
 "note": "SPEC 11.29. The 28 states and 8 union territories of Natural Earth 1:10m admin-1, `admin = India`, listed largest polygon first, which is the order the map tries to place their names in. `lat` and `lon` are where the unit's name is written and are inside the unit, and `fit` is how much room there is to write it there (SPEC 11.31). `code` is Natural Earth's own `postal` field, shown instead of the name wherever the name does not fit inside the unit itself. `city` is the one town the map labels in that unit -- its capital where Natural Earth marks one inside the unit, otherwise the largest town inside it by population -- and its `lat` and `lon` are the 0.25 degree square the page shows, never the town's own position. Built by scripts/build_towns.py.",
 "fit": {
  "aspects": [
   2.0,
   4.0,
   6.0,
   9.0,
   13.0,
   18.0,
   25.0
  ],
  "note": "SPEC 11.31. Each unit's `fit` is half the height, in degrees of latitude, of the tallest box centred on its label point that is still inside the unit's own polygon, for a box of each of these shapes in turn -- the shape being its width over its height in degrees. The page draws a unit's full name only where the name's own box passes this test, and its two letter code everywhere else, so a name is never written across a neighbour. Measured by binary search over shapely's `within`, to a tenth of a second of arc, at the rounded label point above."
 },
